<title>USA: Lebanon, Ore., health deal ylds 6.625 pct in 2021.</title>
<headline>Lebanon, Ore., health deal ylds 6.625 pct in 2021.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seattle Northwest Securities Corp said Tuesday it tentatively priced $6 million Lebanon, Ore., Hospital Facilities Authority gross revenue bonds, series 1996, for the Mid-Valley Healthcare Wiley Creek project, at a top yield of 6.625 percent in 2021.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>CITY OF LEBANON, OREGON, HOSPITAL FACILITIES AUTHORITY</p>
<p>GROSS REVENUE BONDS, SERIES 1996</p>
<p>MID-VALLEY HEALTHCARE WILEY CREEK PROJECT</p>
<p>$6,000,000*</p>
<p>NOT RATED</p>
<p>EXPECTED DELIVERY: 10/9/96</p>
<p>DATED 10/196</p>
<p>CALL FEATURE: 4/1/2006 @ 100</p>
<p>FIRST COUPON: 4/1/97</p>
<p>    4/1	     Amount	  Coupon	Price</p>
<p>    Maturity	(mln)	   (pct)	 (% of par)</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    1998	    $0.115	  4.50	  4.50</p>
<p>    1999	    $0.120	  4.75	  4.75</p>
<p>    2000	    $0.125	  5.00	  5.00</p>
<p>    2001	    $0.140	  5.25	  5.25</p>
<p>    2002	    $0.145	  5.50	  5.50</p>
<p>    2003	    $0.155	  5.75	  5.75</p>
<p>    2011	    $1.615	  6.375	 6.536</p>
<p>CALLABLE 4/1/98 UNTIL 4/1/99 @ 100 - ONE TIME SPECIAL CALL</p>
<p>    2021	    $3.585	  6.50	  6.625</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
